  "strings": {
    "en": {
      "p13_t1_title": "Prolonged phonation - /aaa/",
      "p13_t1_instr1": "<bold>Take a deep breath and sustain the vowel /aaa/ in one breath as long and as steadily as possible. The phonation should last at least 10 seconds.\nI will now play you an example.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press PLAY EXAMPLE to play the example.</italic>",
      "p13_t1_instr2": "<bold>Start now.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press the START button to begin recording. Wait until the participant is out of breath and then press STOP.\nDo not stop the participant; let them phonate as long as possible.\nIf the phonation is shorter than 10 seconds, encourage the participant to prolong it. Changing the pitch or lowering the loudness of the phonation often helps.</italic>",
      "p13_t2_title": "PATAKA",
      "p13_t2_instr1": "<bold>Please repeat the following syllables after me: /pa/-/ta/-/ka/.</bold>\n\n<italic>Say the syllables slowly, firmly and with clear pauses. Once the participant says the syllables correctly, continue with the next instruction:</italic>\n\n<bold>Take a deep breath before the task, then repeat these syllables as fast and as precisely as possible until I stop you. I will now play an example.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press PLAY EXAMPLE to play the example.</italic>",
      "p13_t2_instr2": "<bold>Start now.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press the START button to begin recording. The required number of repetitions is at least 12 triplets of /pa-ta-ka/. Then press STOP button to end the recording.\nThe repetition rate should keep the individual syllables intelligible (no mumbling!).</italic>",
      "p13_t3_title": "Reading - The North Wind and the Sun",
      "p13_t3_instr1": "<bold>Now I will ask you to read a short passage of text. If you use glasses, please put them on now.</bold>\n\n<italic>Give the participant the READING TEXT - The North Wind and the Sun.\nOffer the participant a text with a suitable font size.</italic>",
      "p13_t3_instr2": "<bold>Start now.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press the START button to begin recording. Wait until the participant finishes the task, then press the STOP button to end the recording.</italic>",
      "p13_t3_instr3": "The North Wind and the Sun were disputing which was the stronger, when a traveller, came along wrapped in a warm cloak. They agreed that the one who first succeeded in, making the traveller take his cloak off should be considered stronger than the other. Then the North Wind blew as hard as he could, but the more he blew the more closely did the traveller fold his cloak around him, and at last the North Wind gave up the attempt. Then the Sun shone out warmly, and immediately the traveller took off his cloak. And so the North Wind was obliged to confess that the Sun was the stronger of the two.",
      "p13_t4_title": "Monologue - Free narration",
      "p13_t4_instr1": "<bold>Now I will ask you to talk to me continuously about something for at least 90 seconds. The choice of topic is entirely up to you. You can talk, for example, about your interests, your family or your work.</bold>\n\n<italic>The required length of the recorded monologue is at least 90 seconds.</italic>",
      "p13_t4_instr2": "<bold>You can start whenever you are ready.</bold>\n\n<italic>Press the START button to begin recording and the STOP button at the end of the task to end the recording.\nNote the monologue time. If the monologue is short or poor in content, try to extend the topic with follow-up questions or suggest a new topic. In the worst case, you can switch to a so-called guided discussion. In a guided discussion, try to ask open questions that require a long answer. The total monologue time, without long pauses and examiner questions, should be at least 90 seconds.</italic>",
      "p13_t5_title": "RBD-SQ",
      "p13_t5_q1_text": "I sometimes have very vivid dreams.",
      "p13_t5_q1_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q1_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q2_text": "My dreams frequently have an aggressive or action-packed content.",
      "p13_t5_q2_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q2_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q3_text": "The dream contents mostly match my nocturnal behavior.",
      "p13_t5_q3_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q3_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q4_text": "I know that my arms or legs move when I sleep.",
      "p13_t5_q4_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q4_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q5_text": "It thereby happened that I (almost) hurt my bed partner or myself.",
      "p13_t5_q5_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q5_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q6_text": "I have or had the following phenomena during my dreams: speaking, shouting, swearing, laughing loudly",
      "p13_t5_q6_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q6_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q7_text": "I have or had the following phenomena during my dreams: sudden limb movements, “fights”",
      "p13_t5_q7_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q7_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q8_text": "I have or had the following phenomena during my dreams: gestures, complex movements, that are useless during sleep, e.g., to wave, to salute, to frighten mosquitoes, falls off the bed",
      "p13_t5_q8_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q8_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q9_text": "I have or had the following phenomena during my dreams: things that fell down around the bed, e.g., bedside lamp, book, glasses",
      "p13_t5_q9_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q9_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q10_text": "It happens that my movements awake me.",
      "p13_t5_q10_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q10_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q11_text": "After awakening I mostly remember the content of my dreams well.",
      "p13_t5_q11_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q11_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q12_text": "My sleep is frequently disturbed.",
      "p13_t5_q12_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q12_o2": "No",
      "p13_t5_q13_text": "I have/had a disease of the nervous system (e.g., stroke, head trauma, Parkinsonism, RLS, narcolepsy, depression, epilepsy, inflammatory disease of the brain).",
      "p13_t5_q13_o1": "Yes",
      "p13_t5_q13_o2": "No",
